# Many-into-one consolidation

## Top rule

**Look for opportunities to consolidate components or complexity whenever the opportunity arises.** Before adding a new local splash, gate, chrome row, or one-off helper, scan for an existing copy of the same pattern. Prefer one shared component (or one shared contract) over a third parallel implementation.

Do this on ordinary feature work, not only when the user says “consolidate.” If you notice two or more copies of the same UI or behavior, name it and fold them — or queue it in the list below if it is out of scope for the current change.

## When you consolidate

In the **same change set**, append a **Rule of thumb** at the **top** of the list (newest first). The entry is the reusable lesson, not a changelog of files.

```markdown
### YYYY-MM-DD — <short pattern name>

**Many:** what was duplicated (count + where, in one line).
**One:** the shared component or contract that replaced it.
**Thumb:** what a future agent should look for next time.
```

## Rule of thumb list

### 2026-10-14 — Enter splash (copy + Continue)

**Many:** Local `*Splash` functions in Coordinate prompt, Photo Critique, and NPM Audit — same centered sentence and Continue.
**One:** [`src/components/EnterSplash.tsx`](src/components/EnterSplash.tsx) (`EnterSplashConfig`). Optional `youtubeId`, optional `date`. Fields live in JSON next to the demo (e.g. `enterSplash.json`), not hardcoded in the component. MediaModal archive splash is still a local gate — candidate to join later.
**Thumb:** A modal or demo that opens with a sentence and **Continue** should use `EnterSplash`, not a new local splash. Video and date are config fields, not one-off overlays.
